HST Office: Windows media playback no longer leaves MFPlay calling into a deleted player.

A Player gets a new MFPlay player for every view that shows it (createPlayerWindow, the video Window, start()
for background sounds), and InitializeWindow released the previous one without IMFPMediaPlayer::Shutdown().
MFPlay keeps its own reference to the callback and keeps posting events from the message loop until Shutdown;
the Player itself is deleted by its UNO reference count, which ignores the COM one. A later event then called
OnMediaPlayerEvent on a deleted Player: access violation inside MFPlay.DLL dispatched from the office's
message loop (Slides on Windows 11, 1.0.2, 70-90 s after opening two presentations). Every release now shuts
the player down first (ReleaseMediaPlayer), the destructor stops MFPlay before destroying the window it
renders into, and OnClose no longer posts WM_QUIT to the office's main thread (sample-code leftover that could
end a modal loop running at that moment). Not fixed upstream (26.8.3, master 2026-11).

